{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner decision on hosted MCP opt-in (follows 8904bf5b and 92d54432; main 9d53b9e7, check 38b63328).\nEvidence, from queries at 09:19: the Analytics Engine dataset artroom_metrics_v1 holds no point with schema mcp-metrics-v1 in the last 90 days. The same dataset holds 2,075,235 other points in the last 30 days, so the sink works. The MCP metric wiring landed on 17 October (3fb7d5cd). dap-grow has run it since then, and artroom-scope and dap-demo since their 23 October deploys. So no hosted agent made a tool call on these Workers in that time. dap-lending binds no MCP namespaces, so its endpoint is already closed.\nDecision: leave MCP_ENABLED unset on dap-grow, dap-demo and artroom-scope at their next deploy. Hosted MCP is then closed on all four Workers, and no Worker has MCP_TOOL_ADDITIONS. A slice that needs hosted agents (for example the hosted Counter agent teams) names the Worker and the tool additions, and the planner opens the endpoint in that slice's deploy record. With the endpoint closed, no live bearer needs a renewal at the R5 cutover in 855dd86d.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}